# SAC FROM c0, PRIVILEGED CRITIC, GOAL KEPT FIXED -- WITH NO SPAWN INSIDE A JUNCTION AND THE ACTOR RELEASED
# FROM THE FIRST UPDATE (user 2026-11-14: "ensure the agent does not spawn in middle of junction", "also
# release c0 as soon as it starts").
# = slurm/local_frl_c0actor_privcritic_t01_ar2_keepgoal.env with ONLY:
#   1. ORIGIN_NOT_IN_JUNCTION=1 (slurm/patch_rlib_origin_not_in_junction.py, applied to the snapshot's
#      rlib_integration): the junction-biased origin walked 5-25 m back from a waypoint INSIDE a junction,
#      which in a wide junction is still junction interior. It is now walked further back onto ordinary road.
#      TRAINING ONLY: the scoring overlay does not set it, so the fixed scoring episodes are unchanged.
#   2. FRL_ACTOR_FREEZE=0: the actor trains from the first update (decision 1,000) instead of after 15,000
#      critic-only decisions. RISK ON RECORD: every earlier start from c0 without a freeze collapsed within
#      about 1,000 actor updates; those runs had an image critic and the moving-goal defect.
export FRL_ACTOR_FREEZE=${FRL_ACTOR_FREEZE:-0}
. "$REPO/slurm/local_frl_c0actor_privcritic_t01_ar2_keepgoal.env"
export ORIGIN_NOT_IN_JUNCTION=1
